    "updated_at": "2020-05-17T21:52:38Z",
    "body": "Be careful on Windows with std::fs::Permissions.\r\nPer https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.set_permissions.html, it only uses the GetFileAttributes and  is a really bad friend to determine if a directory is read-only. \r\n\r\nOn Windows, NTFS uses Access Control List detailing user/groups permissions in a very detailed way (for more information, please consider reading https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/file-security-and-access-rights).\r\n\r\nYour best chance to determine if the user has write access into a directory is to perform an AccessCheck (https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/securitybaseapi/nf-securitybaseapi-accesscheck) on the current thread's token. \r\n\r\n\r\n ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
